    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the region-to-timezone derivation so the owner response now includes an IANA `timezone` field derived from locality/region.\n\nThree changes, following the existing `locality` pattern exactly:\n\n1. **`OwnerRegion.java`** \u2014 added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneOf(customerCode)` method that resolves the region from the customer code and maps it to the IANA name (`null` when the region is absent or unknown).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` and a `timezone(owner)` default delegating to `OwnerRegion.timezoneOf`, mirroring how `locality` is wired.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (owner in Sydney \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) now passes, and the full suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
